After slogging through Gehennom, defeating the mighty Wizard and the
not-so-mighty Vamp, and standing at the gate to Moloch's, Tjr2 the
Speedy went to see his/her mentor Neferet the Green. Surely, after all
these deeds, a mighty soul-eating warrior would save wizardfolk from
the dreaded Dark One in a pinch. He/She was sent back with a
condescending pat on the head.

Tjr3 the Well-Behaved reported similar problems on his path to
literate ascension. By far the hardest part was convincing his
stepmother that he wasn't a child anymore.

I propose: Any character carrying both the non-cursed, candled
Candelabrum and the non-cursed Book of the Dead should be allowed on
the Quest if he/she/it is at least as well-aligned as when they
entered the dungeon.


